WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.127
Week 32: Work, Technology, and Formal Communication. summarize a meeting write a professional message explain a technical problem and next action

2
00:00:10.127 --> 00:00:18.143
Cultural lens. Email openings, messaging norms, workplace hierarchy, remote work, and technology access.

3
00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:30.577
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:30.577 --> 00:00:42.584
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:51.797
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:51.797 --> 00:01:26.695
Model language. El correo electrónico suele empezar con un saludo formal. — Email usually starts with a formal greeting. El mensaje instantáneo es más informal. — Instant messaging is more informal. El trabajo remoto cambia la comunicación diaria. — Remote work changes daily communication. El acceso tecnológico no es igual en todas partes. — Technological access isn't the same everywhere. La jerarquía influye en el tono del mensaje. — Hierarchy influences the tone of the message.

7
00:01:26.695 --> 00:01:36.849
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
